class Runny < Formula
  desc "Observable macOS GitHub Actions runner daemon on Virtualization.framework"
  homepage "https://github.com/bojanrajkovic/runny"
  version "${VERSION}"
  url "${URL}"
  sha256 "${SHA}"
  license "MIT"

  depends_on :macos
  depends_on arch: :arm64

  def install
    bin.install "runnyd"
    bin.install "runnyctl"
  end

  # This formula is delivery-only: it installs the binaries, not a service. A
  # `brew services` block can only create a per-user LaunchAgent (Homebrew's DSL
  # has no run-as-user field), and the headless install is a non-root system
  # LaunchDaemon — created by `runnyctl install-daemon`, which needs the
  # privileged dscl/launchctl steps a formula can't perform. See docs/deploy.md.

  def caveats
    <<~TEXT
      This installs the runnyd and runnyctl binaries only — it does not register
      a service. The binary ships signed with com.apple.security.virtualization.

      To run runnyd headless as a non-root system LaunchDaemon:

          sudo runnyctl install-daemon

      One privileged step creates a dedicated service account and the system
      LaunchDaemon; the daemon then runs unprivileged. Afterward write the config
      at /Library/Application Support/runny/config.yaml (your account has
      write access via an inheriting ACL) and the daemon comes up on its next
      restart; verify with `runnyctl doctor`. A launchd-started daemon of any uid
      is auto-allowed Local Network access — no GUI prompt.

      For a desktop, per-user install instead, use the Runny app. See
      docs/deploy.md.
    TEXT
  end

  test do
    assert_match version.to_s, shell_output("#{bin}/runnyctl version")
  end
end
